<h1>Monday Playbook</h1>
<div class="dates">Your picks from the forensic report · Week of Mon 17 Aug -&gt; Fri 21 Aug 2026</div></div>
<p class="pk-intro">Every concrete play from the report, one card each. Tap <b>Shadow</b>, <b>Live</b>, or <b>Skip</b> for each. Your picks save automatically — when you're done, hit <b>Copy my picks</b> or <b>Send to Telegram</b> and they come back to me for the shadow-vs-live conversation before Monday. <b>Refuted &amp; exploratory plays can't go Live</b> until they survive a week in shadow — that guardrail is built in.</p>
<div class="pk-group">✅ Act on these — survived proof &amp; real bugs</div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="delete-weekend-flatten-timer-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">SATURDAY #1 · Front page (how the open position ended); Part 1.6 §5; the unit&#x27;s own journal, which is the arbiter here rather than any desk instrument. · DELETE gazbot7-weekend-flatten.timer — it is still armed and it fires again on Sunday</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">&lt;code&gt;systemctl disable --now gazbot7-weekend-flatten.timer&lt;/code&gt; and remove the unit file. It was built as a one-shot for a position that no longer exists, and it is the only row on this card with a date attached.</div><div class="pk-meta">The unit is written to self-disable once the venue reads flat — but it dies on a &lt;code&gt;PermissionError&lt;/code&gt; before it ever reads the venue, so it has never disabled itself. &lt;code&gt;systemctl list-timers&lt;/code&gt; has it next elapsing &lt;strong&gt;Sunday 2026-08-30 22:00Z&lt;/strong&gt;, then every minute to 23:59Z. What it does when it runs is re-arm the day rider and write a &lt;em&gt;bare-stamp&lt;/em&gt; claim through the operator-button path — and a bare stamp means &lt;strong&gt;claim everything&lt;/strong&gt;. Against whatever happens to be open that night, on a shared netted account, that is the 08-06 cascade with a timer on it.  ·  A recovery job that outlives the incident it was built for is not a safety net, it is an unowned actor with write authority. This one cannot even report that it failed: the page() call sits BELOW the file write that kills it.  ·  The number: 119 firings on 2026-08-23, 0 orders placed, 0 pages sent. Next elapse Sun 2026-08-30 22:00Z. Journal: 105 gateway failures then 14 PermissionError.  ·  Proven wrong by: &lt;code&gt;systemctl list-timers | grep weekend-flatten&lt;/code&gt; returns nothing, and &lt;code&gt;systemctl is-enabled gazbot7-weekend-flatten.timer&lt;/code&gt; says &lt;code&gt;disabled&lt;/code&gt; or the unit is gone.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="day-rider-protective-stop-3atr-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">SATURDAY #2 · Part 1.5 disposition (LIVE) and Part 1.6 §3b — the corrected rider-stop grid, raced on every day rather than only the losing one. · Put a protective stop on the day rider&#x27;s own book at 3.0×ATR</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Add a venue-resting protective stop to &lt;code&gt;day_rider.py&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;strong&gt;3.0×ATR&lt;/strong&gt; from entry. Not 1.5× — that width was this report&#x27;s first answer and it is wrong.</div><div class="pk-meta">The rider is a second book on the same IB account and it has never had a stop. Re-racing ALL SIX of the week&#x27;s rider entries at seven widths, rather than just the losing one, moves the answer: the closed book as traded is −$272.00; at 3.0×ATR it is &lt;strong&gt;+$195.70&lt;/strong&gt;, the only positive cell and the only one that keeps all three winners. 1.5×ATR — the first pick — is −$388.90 and keeps one. Cause of death for the tighter width is winners-retention, not expectancy.  ·  It is the week&#x27;s highest-value change and the week&#x27;s whole loss is one unstopped position. Every width tested closes Friday&#x27;s four lots within nineteen minutes of entry, six and a half hours before the gateway stopped answering — so the stop is upstream of the wedge, not a victim of it.  ·  The number: +$468 against the week as traded (as-traded −$272.00 → +$195.70 at 3.0×ATR), on 6 entries × 7 widths.  ·  Proven wrong by: A resting stop order visible on the venue within 60s of a rider entry, and &lt;code&gt;day_rider_state.json&lt;/code&gt; carrying its price. Not a soft stop in code.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="standdown-to-a-file-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">SATURDAY #3 · Part 2.6 §4 and its disposition (LIVE, named a Saturday item). · Make the tournament standdown a FILE that every writer checks</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Move &lt;code&gt;TOURNAMENT_STOOD_DOWN&lt;/code&gt; out of &lt;code&gt;router_tick_durable.py&lt;/code&gt; and into a state file, and make &lt;code&gt;open_hour_watch.py&lt;/code&gt; — and any future writer — read it before writing a switch.</div><div class="pk-meta">The standdown is a router-LOCAL variable. It only stops the ROUTER writing &lt;code&gt;on&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;open_hour_watch.py&lt;/code&gt; is a second writer with off→on authority and zero standdown awareness, and on Friday it armed &lt;code&gt;abs_veto_short&lt;/code&gt; straight through the standing operator standdown. The only reason that cost nothing is that the tape produced no signal in the 2m15s window before it was benched again.  ·  A safety state that one of its two writers cannot see is not a safety state. This is a $0 incident purely by luck, and luck is not a control.  ·  The number: 1 unauthorised arm on 2026-08-21, 2m15s wide, $0 by luck. &lt;code&gt;open-hour-watch.service&lt;/code&gt;&#x27;s own unit file says it must NEVER write &lt;code&gt;gate_switches.env&lt;/code&gt;; it has written since 08-05.  ·  Proven wrong by: Set the standdown, then force an &lt;code&gt;open_hour_watch&lt;/code&gt; arm condition and confirm it refuses and logs the refusal. A test that cannot be shown to fail is not a test.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="delete-carveout-header-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">SATURDAY #4 · Part 2.6 §5 and its disposition (LIVE). · Delete the five expired carve-outs from gate_switches.env&#x27;s comment header</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Open &lt;code&gt;data/gate_switches.env&lt;/code&gt; and delete the five dated instruction lines in its header. Deleting the lines is the only thing that closes a carve-out.</div><div class="pk-meta">&lt;code&gt;switch_notes()&lt;/code&gt; splices the top 45 comment lines of that file into EVERY router prompt, labelled ACTIVE, and nothing prunes them. Five are in there now, the oldest thirteen days old. Four are past their own stated expiry. &lt;strong&gt;The 2026-08-09 line is the dangerous one: it asserts that &lt;code&gt;abs_veto_short&lt;/code&gt; IS ARMED BY DEFAULT&lt;/strong&gt; — which directly contradicts the standing operator standdown the router is currently enforcing, on the same gate that &lt;code&gt;open_hour_watch.py&lt;/code&gt; armed through that standdown on Friday.  ·  A carve-out comment never expires and a zero-mention streak is not a fix. Two of the five have been restated to the router 106 and 66 times out of 1,425 ticks; the other three sit there quietly and would be read the moment the tape produces the situation they describe.  ·  The number: 5 instructions spliced as ACTIVE, oldest 13d 1h. Restated 106 and 66 times in 1,425 ticks; three at 0 of 1,425 — which is a dormant instruction, not a closed one.  ·  Proven wrong by: &lt;code&gt;head -45 data/gate_switches.env&lt;/code&gt; shows no dated instruction lines, and the next router tick&#x27;s prompt carries no ACTIVE carve-out block.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="core-health-flat-venue-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">SATURDAY #5 · Part 2.6 §6 and disposition (LIVE); Part 1 disposition (FAULT). · Point core_health.flat at the venue position, or rename it tournament_flat</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Either make &lt;code&gt;core_health.flat&lt;/code&gt; read the venue position line, or rename the field so nobody reads it as a desk-wide safety signal again.</div><div class="pk-meta">The field is tournament-scoped. It said the desk was flat while the venue was long four lots, and the router repeated that reading for 137 of 141 consecutive ticks while &lt;code&gt;updatePortfolio&lt;/code&gt; in the same journal read &lt;code&gt;position=4.0 … unrealizedPNL=−950.27&lt;/code&gt;.  ·  This is the instrument that should have caught the whole incident and it read green throughout. A flag that is right about one book and silent about the other is worse than no flag, because it is the one people check.  ·  The number: 137 of 141 router ticks called a live four-lot position flat.  ·  Proven wrong by: Open a 1-lot rider position by hand and confirm &lt;code&gt;core_health.flat&lt;/code&gt; goes false. If it stays true, the rename is the honest option.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="mgc-depth-mid-bars-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #1 · Movement 3 §8 (gold, in its own right); the MGC dossier §3 and §12.1 in the appendix. · ★ Build the depth-mid bar source into the MGC shadow — the gating item for all of gold</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Point the MGC shadow service&#x27;s minute-bar builder at the &lt;strong&gt;depth mid&lt;/strong&gt; instead of at trades, and keep the existing trade-bar arms alive as &lt;code&gt;*_tradebar&lt;/code&gt; controls so the difference is visible rather than asserted. Nothing else on the gold line is worth doing first.</div><div class="pk-meta">Last week&#x27;s shadowed gold gate has been live since Monday and is losing: &lt;strong&gt;−$1,196 across 80 trades in seven days, all three arms red&lt;/strong&gt;. The lab replay of the same seven days makes +$512. The cause is the input tape: the research builds one-minute bars from the depth mid (which updates every 250ms whether or not anything trades), the service builds them from trades, and gold prints sparsely — so a sixty-minute high on one is not the sixty-minute high on the other. Hold everything else constant and change only the tape: depth-mid bars n=56 → &lt;strong&gt;+$172 (+$3.06/tr)&lt;/strong&gt;; trade bars n=53 → &lt;strong&gt;−$475 (−$8.96/tr)&lt;/strong&gt;. The sign flips on the bar source alone.  ·  This is a plumbing mismatch between lab and production, not a research failure, and the fix is mechanical: the service already holds a &lt;code&gt;DepthFeed&lt;/code&gt; connection to gold&#x27;s book because the liquidity filter needs it, so it already has the bid and the ask. Until it lands, no gold cell should be promoted and none is being proposed.  ·  The number: Live shadow −$1,196 / 80 trades vs lab +$512 on the same days. Bar-source A/B on the six days both tapes cover: +$3.06/tr vs −$8.96/tr.  ·  Proven wrong by: Both arms present in &lt;code&gt;data/shadow_mgc.db&lt;/code&gt; under distinct names, and a week of forward trades where the depth-mid arm and the &lt;code&gt;*_tradebar&lt;/code&gt; control diverge in the predicted direction.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="shadowvariant-missing-fields-0821" data-default="live"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #2 · Movement 3 §9 item 5; the RIDER_ALL dossier §11 in the appendix, which lists all three blockers with the one-line fix for each. · Add atr_min, a wrapping clock window and an ER10 gate param to ShadowVariant</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">Three small changes to &lt;code&gt;src/gazbot7/shadow.py&lt;/code&gt;: (1) &lt;code&gt;gate_board&lt;/code&gt;&#x27;s window test becomes &lt;code&gt;inw = (lo &amp;lt;= h &amp;lt; hi) if lo &amp;lt; hi else (h &amp;gt;= lo or h &amp;lt; hi)&lt;/code&gt; so a 21:00→07:00 window can exist at all; (2) &lt;code&gt;ShadowVariant&lt;/code&gt; gains an &lt;code&gt;atr_min&lt;/code&gt;, defaulted to 0.0 so nothing existing changes; (3) an &lt;code&gt;er_win_min&lt;/code&gt; that reads the ENTRY WINDOW&#x27;s efficiency rather than ER30.</div><div class="pk-meta">All three are blockers on shadowing anything from this movement honestly. A rule that is a BAND cannot be expressed with only a ceiling. A wrapping clock window is never true, so an overnight arm silently never fires. And &lt;code&gt;ShadowVariant.er_min&lt;/code&gt; reads ER30 — substituting it for the 10-minute ER FLIPS the held-out leg from +$5.34 to −$2.25 a trade and turns both controls positive, i.e. it is a different hypothesis wearing the same name.  ·  ★ This is exactly how &lt;code&gt;rider_w5&lt;/code&gt; came to be quoted at +$19.29 while making −$28.84. An arm shipped AROUND a missing field records a different strategy under the intended name, and nothing downstream can tell.  ·  The number: ER30 substituted for ER10 flips the held-out leg +$5.34/tr → −$2.25/tr and reverses both controls.  ·  Proven wrong by: A unit test that an arm with &lt;code&gt;hh_lo=21, hh_hi=7&lt;/code&gt; fires at 23:00Z and not at 12:00Z, and one that &lt;code&gt;atr_min&lt;/code&gt; excludes a below-band fire.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
<div class="pk-card" data-id="census-flow-bucket-phase-0821" data-default="shadow"><div class="pk-top"><span class="pk-ref">BUILD #3 · Movement 3 §4 (the vocabulary table) and §9 item 3; the UNCLASS dossier §13. · ★ Fix the census&#x27;s flow-bucket phase — 21 of 68 labels move on it alone</span><span class="pill v-verified">✓ VERIFIED</span></div><div class="pk-play">In &lt;code&gt;scripts/run_census.py&lt;/code&gt;, snap the flow window&#x27;s slide to the CLOCK rather than to the array index.</div><div class="pk-meta">21 of 68 run labels change on bucket phase alone, and only 17 of the 68 run timestamps are minute-aligned in the first place. This is the mechanism behind the divergence between the two census freezes this cycle — 70 runs / 65 sat out / $9,986 became 68 / 62 / $9,610 — which is why Movement 2 carries a red banner.  ·  Every hunt this desk scopes by cluster inherits this error, and it is a real bug with a one-line character rather than a modelling judgement.  ·  The number: 21 of 68 labels phase-dependent; 17 of 68 run timestamps minute-aligned; two freezes of the same week differ by 2 runs and $376 of ceiling.  ·  Proven wrong by: Re-freeze the census twice with the bucket origin offset by 30s and get the same 68 labels both times.</div><div class="pk-opts"><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="shadow">Shadow</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="live">Live</button><button class="pk-opt" data-mode="skip">Skip</button></div></div>
